      "seq": 102,
      "player": "Sonnet Hype",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Perfect! Now I have 5 lands total (3 untapped). I can:\n\
- Cast Sage's Reverie for 4 mana (but still have 0 Auras attached, so it's weak)\n\
- Cast Befuddle for 3 mana (but there's no target worth hitting)\n\
- Just attack!\n\
\n\
Wait, Sage's Reverie costs {3}{W}, which is 4 mana. I have 2 Plains and 3 Islands. That's 2 White sources and 3 Blue sources. I can cast it!\n\
\n\
But is it worth it? It would:\n\
- Draw 0 cards (no Auras attached)\n\
- Give +1/+1 to enchanted creature\n\
- Trigger Wayfarer's Constellation (+1/+1 to another creature)\n\
\n\
So for 4 mana I get +1/+1 permanently on one creature, and +1/+1 temporarily on another. That's... okay? Not great.\n\
\n\
I think I should just ATTACK! My creatures are:\n\
- Nebelgast Herald 2/1 Flying\n\
- Pious Wayfarer 1/2\n\
- Spirited Companion 2/2\n\
\n\
That's 5 power! Let's move to combat!\n\
\n\
TIME TO ATTACK! LET'S GO TO COMBAT!",
