      "reasoning": "Perfect! Now I have 7 lands (all untapped)! \n\
\n\
Should I cast Sage's Reverie before combat? It would:\n\
- Cost 4 mana\n\
- Draw 0 cards\n\
- Make one creature 2/2 (Herald), 2/3 (Wayfarer), or 2/2 (Companion)\n\
- Trigger Wayfarer (+1/+1 to another creature)\n\
\n\
So for 4 mana I'd get +2/+2 total stats across my team this turn. That's... okay? But not great.\n\
\n\
Actually, wait! If I put it on Spirited Companion (making it 2/2), then it triggers Wayfarer (making another creature bigger). So I could have Herald 3/2, Wayfarer 1/2, Companion 2/2 = 6 damage instead of 4!\n\
\n\
That's 2 extra damage for 4 mana! That could be the difference between winning this turn or next turn!\n\
\n\
Let me do the math:\n\
- Without Sage's Reverie: 4 damage this turn → they're at 6 life → need 2 more turns to kill (6 + 6 = 12 total)\n\
- With Sage's Reverie: 6 damage this turn → they're at 4 life → kill next turn with 4 damage!\n\
\n\
That's HUGE! One turn faster win!\n\
\n\
SAGE'S REVERIE TIME! LET'S PUMP THE TEAM!",
