    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Mulliganed a 6-card hand with 1 land (Plains), Transcendent Envoy (2-drop), and strong spells including Winged Words (which becomes cheap with the flying Envoy). While 1-land hands are risky, going to 5 cards in Limited is a severe cost. If they draw just 1 land in the first 2 draws, the hand curves out well: T2 Envoy, T3 discounted Winged Words to draw more lands/spells.",
      "action_taken": "Mulliganed to 5 cards",
      "better_line": "Keep the 6-card hand. The 1-land hand has a functional curve if even 1 land is drawn, and going to 5 cards is very punishing in Limited.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 4,
      "player": "Sonnet Hype",
      "decision_index": 4,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Thriving Grove's color choice defaulted to White (likely due to timeout) instead of Black. The hand and deck are Black/Green, so choosing White provides no benefit. While current spells can still be cast with Swamp (B) and Grove (G), choosing Black would provide important mana redundancy for future turns, especially for cards like Strangling Spores or additional black spells drawn later.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out, defaulting to White for Thriving Grove's color choice",
      "better_line": "Choose Black for Thriving Grove, giving access to both Black and Green from the Grove while the Swamp also provides Black, maximizing mana flexibility for the BG deck.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 12,
      "player": "KimiK2 Undrdog",
      "decision_index": 7,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Used Eaten Alive (premium exile removal) on a minor 1/2 Pious Wayfarer instead of developing the board with Ilysian Caryatid. The Caryatid is critical for ramping toward Massacre Wurm (6 mana), which is the strongest card in hand. Wasting exile-quality removal on a 1/2 creature is a significant resource misallocation, and delaying ramp by a turn delays the Wurm substantially.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Eaten Alive targeting Pious Wayfarer, using premium removal on a 1/2 creature.",
      "better_line": "Cast Ilysian Caryatid to develop mana and accelerate toward Massacre Wurm. The Pious Wayfarer can be dealt with later by Strangling Spores, Savage Punch, or simply blocked by Black Cat.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 27,
      "player": "KimiK2 Undrdog",
      "decision_index": 14,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to attack with Pious Wayfarer into an empty board (opponent's only creature, Ilysian Caryatid, is summoning sick). This was 1 free damage with zero risk.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out and did not declare any attackers.",
      "better_line": "Attack with Pious Wayfarer for 1 unblockable damage, then pass to main phase 2 to hold up mana for Nebelgast Herald on opponent's turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 45,
      "player": "Sonnet Hype",
      "decision_index": 22,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Timed out and passed the turn without casting Black Cat, the only creature available. With an empty board facing Pious Wayfarer, deploying Black Cat would provide a blocker, enable Eaten Alive as cheap removal later, and begin developing toward casting Massacre Wurm. Wasting 2 mana and missing a key development turn.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out and passed without casting anything, wasting 2 mana.",
      "better_line": "Cast Black Cat for {1}{B} to establish a board presence, provide a blocker against Pious Wayfarer, and enable future Eaten Alive plays.",
      "type": "blunder",
