    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Timed out in precombat main with strong plays available. Savage Punch with indestructible Rhonas (getting +2/+2 from Ferocious) would kill Nebelgast Herald for free since Rhonas is indestructible and takes no lasting damage from the fight. The Herald is the opponent's best creature (flash, flying, tap ability). Strangling Spores could also kill any of the opponent's creatures.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out and passed priority without casting any spells.",
      "better_line": "Cast Savage Punch targeting Rhonas and Nebelgast Herald. Rhonas fights as a 7/7 deathtouch indestructible, killing the Herald with zero risk. This removes the opponent's best evasive threat and the tap trigger that has been keeping Rhonas locked down.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 177,
      "player": "KimiK2 Undrdog",
      "decision_index": 76,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Passed precombat main phase with Savage Punch available to kill Nebelgast Herald for free (Rhonas is indestructible with Ferocious active). While they could theoretically cast it postcombat, there's no strategic benefit to waiting since Rhonas can't attack anyway. The 2/1 flyer has been a damage source and removing it is pure value.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority in precombat main phase without casting any spells",
      "better_line": "Cast Savage Punch targeting Rhonas fighting Nebelgast Herald (2/1 flyer) — Rhonas gets +2/+2 from Ferocious, is indestructible, and kills the flyer for free. This removes the most threatening creature on board.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 177,
      "player": "KimiK2 Undrdog",
      "decision_index": 76,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Put the Pious Wayfarer constellation +1/+1 buff on Spirited Companion (1/1 ground creature) instead of Nebelgast Herald (3/2 flyer). The Herald has flying and is the primary damage dealer against an opponent at 10 life with Rhonas blocking the ground. Buffing the Herald to 4/3 flying would deal 1 extra evasive damage this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Targeted Spirited Companion with the constellation +1/+1 trigger",
      "better_line": "Target Nebelgast Herald with the +1/+1 to maximize flying damage this combat, pushing 4 damage through the air instead of 3",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 193,
      "player": "Sonnet Hype",
      "decision_index": 84,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "By passing with the Sage's Reverie draw trigger on the stack, KimiK2 allowed the opponent to draw a card. Casting Strangling Spores on Spirited Companion in response would have killed it before the trigger resolved, causing Sage's Reverie to fall off. The draw trigger would then count 0 Auras attached to creatures, denying the card draw while also removing both Spirited Companion and Sage's Reverie.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, allowing Sage's Reverie's draw trigger to resolve and draw a card.",
      "better_line": "Cast Strangling Spores targeting Spirited Companion (2/2 with Sage's Reverie) in response to the draw trigger. This kills the creature, Sage's Reverie falls off, and the draw trigger resolves drawing 0 cards instead of 1. Two-for-one removal plus card denial.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 197,
      "player": "KimiK2 Undrdog",
      "decision_index": 86,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Rhonas the Indomitable cannot block because the opponent controls no other creature with power 4 or greater. All three creatures (Nebelgast Herald 3/2, Spirited Companion 2/2, Pious Wayfarer 1/2) could attack completely unblocked for 6 damage, taking the opponent from 10 to 4 life. Missing this much free damage against a low-life opponent is game-altering.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out and declared no attackers, dealing 0 damage.",
      "better_line": "Attack with all three creatures (Nebelgast Herald, Spirited Companion, Pious Wayfarer) for 6 unblockable damage, putting the opponent to 4 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 200,
      "player": "Sonnet Hype",
      "decision_index": 87,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Passed on casting Befuddle in response to Strangling Spores killing Nebelgast Herald. The Herald dies regardless (-3/-3 kills a 3/2), but Befuddle could have been cast targeting Rhonas the Indomitable to draw a card (cantrip value) while also temporarily reducing Rhonas to 1/5. The 3 untapped lands (Island, Thriving Isle, Plains) could pay {2}{U}. While saving Befuddle for later has some merit as a combat trick, the card draw now replaces itself and the -4/-0 on Rhonas during an attack step where Sonnet Hype's creatures are attacking has minimal downside.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, allowing Strangling Spores to resolve and kill Nebelgast Herald (and lose Sage's Reverie) without using the available mana.",
      "better_line": "Cast Befuddle targeting Rhonas the Indomitable to draw a card, replacing Befuddle with a fresh draw while also temporarily weakening Rhonas.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 209,
      "player": "Sonnet Hype",
      "decision_index": 91,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Passed on casting Befuddle targeting Rhonas during combat. With 3 untapped lands (exactly {2}{U} available), Befuddle could cantrip while reducing Rhonas to 1/5. The player has no other instant-speed plays, and Thriving Heath can still be played postcombat. While saving Befuddle for defensive use later has some merit, at 20 life the cantrip value of drawing a card now (potentially finding a better answer) likely outweighs saving 4 damage prevention on a future Rhonas attack.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting Befuddle, wasting 3 mana this turn.",
